WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.471
Jennifer Lawrence has all but vanished from
the public eye in recent months, with the

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:08.630
global pandemic responsible for a slew of
movie shutdowns.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:12.400
Even though she appears to be taking a backseat
right now, Lawrence has been working pretty

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.659
much non-stop since she was a teenager.

00:00:15.659 --> 00:00:19.740
It always seems like an urban legend when
you hear that a famous actor was scouted on

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.050
the street, but according to Jennifer Lawrence,
that really happened.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:27.699
She was just 14 years old and visiting New
York City when she was spotted by a modeling

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:28.910
agent.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.119
Lawrence told Vanity Fair in 2013,

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:36.010
"I was playing field hockey and cheerleading
and wanted to be a doctor — but within 20

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.320
minutes, in the cab ride from the hotel room,
I decided I didn't want to be a model, that,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.110
in fact, I wanted to be an actress, and I
would only sign with an agency if they would

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.090
let me audition for commercials and act as
well."

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:51.680
Lawrence's impulsive decision paid off, as
she revealed to Vanity Fair,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:55.552
"And one of them gave me a script, to audition
the next day, and I read the script and it

00:00:55.552 --> 00:00:59.289
was the first time I had that feeling like
I understand this.

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:01.650
This is the first time I've ever understood
anything.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:06.190
[...] I always felt like I sucked at everything,
that I could never find the thing that I liked.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:10.910
I auditioned and I probably sucked, but I
had decided 100 percent that this is what

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.600
I wanted to do."

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:17.940
Despite her knee-jerk reaction to the opportunity,
14 is pretty young to make such a big decision,

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.970
and her career moved faster than anyone could
have anticipated.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:26.460
Making the huge decision to pursue acting
full-time at such a young age would be daunting

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.960
to begin with, but in Lawrence's case, she
gave up something even bigger, when she dropped

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.250
out of middle school, and never earned a high
school diploma.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:39.110
In conversation with Bill Whitaker of CBS
News, Lawrence explained that she never felt

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:43.431
comfortable in school, and revealed that she
had to convince her parents to let her drop

00:01:43.431 --> 00:01:45.740
out and make the leap to full-time acting.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:46.740
Lawrence explained,

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.280
"It's so hard to explain it was just an overwhelming
feeling of, 'I get this.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.950
This is what I was meant to do.'

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:56.570
And to get people to try to understand that
when you're 14 years old.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.540
Wanting to drop out of school and do this
and your parents are just, like, 'You're out

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:01.540
of your mind.'"

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:06.220
"I dropped out of middle school.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:11.319
I don't technically have a GED or a diploma."

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:14.849
Though she said she doesn't regret her choice,
the weight of this decision must have been

00:02:14.849 --> 00:02:17.040
enormous for a young teenager.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.879
Before long, Lawrence's career would skyrocket,
which would put academic pursuits on the back

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:23.799
burner for the foreseeable future.

00:02:24.799 --> 00:02:30.760
In 2010, Jennifer Lawrence's biggest break
came in the form of Winter's Bone, an Ozarks-set

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:36.799
drama that cast Lawrence as a hard-scrabbling
teen trying to protect her family from poverty,

00:02:36.799 --> 00:02:39.989
a harsh winter, and homelessness in the mountain
range.

00:02:39.989 --> 00:02:45.379
As the de facto head of her family, Lawrence
came off as wise beyond her years, and to

00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:51.560
film the role, she endured some pretty harrowing
experiences, including skinning a dead squirrel.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.269
However, her work paid off.

00:02:53.269 --> 00:02:57.299
In the aftermath of the independent film's
release, Lawrence earned widespread acclaim

00:02:57.299 --> 00:03:00.840
and an Academy Award nomination for her work
in the role.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.819
Now one of the hottest rising stars in the
film industry, Lawrence was more visible than

00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:11.739
ever, catapulted into stardom at an insanely
quick pace as well as at a staggeringly young

00:03:11.739 --> 00:03:12.739
age.

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:18.010
After one leading film role, Jennifer Lawrence
became one of the most recognizable faces

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:23.689
in Hollywood, and when she debuted a bombshell
look at the 2011 Academy Awards to celebrate

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:29.329
her nomination for Winter's Bone, it only
contributed to her fast-growing popularity.

00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:33.700
Before long, Lawrence was fielding a ton of
movie offers, and just a few years after her

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.489
first nomination, she made history with her
first win.

00:03:37.489 --> 00:03:42.650
Two years after Winter's Bone, Lawrence starred
alongside Bradley Cooper under the direction

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:48.779
of David O. Russell in the 2012 film Silver
Linings Playbook, and her performance as Tiffany,

00:03:48.779 --> 00:03:53.409
a widow looking for love in all the wrong
places, earned her the most critical accolades

00:03:53.409 --> 00:03:55.069
of her career to date.

00:03:55.069 --> 00:04:00.390
After winning a string of other awards, including
a Golden Globe, Lawrence took home the Academy

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:06.650
Award for Best Actress in early 2013, making
her the second youngest winner in the category.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:11.440
Just one year later, she set a record as the
youngest ever three-time nominee thanks to

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.420
her performance in Russell's American Hustle.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:19.760
Even before she won her Oscar for Silver Linings
Playbook, Lawrence had cemented her status

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:24.410
in Hollywood thanks to major roles in some
of the industry's biggest franchises.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:30.170
In 2011, Lawrence joined the cast of X-Men:
First Class, where she played Mystique, a

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:36.840
role that she would later reprise in 2014's
Days of Future Past, 2016's Apocalypse and

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.940
2019’s Dark Phoenix.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:44.030
However, you may actually know her best from
her starring role as heroine Katniss Everdeen

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:48.950
in the Hunger Games franchise, which spawned
four films and made Lawrence the highest-grossing

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.440
action heroine of all time.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:56.120
Lawrence also partnered with David O. Russell
and Bradley Cooper for several different projects,

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:00.910
including Silver Linings Playbook, American
Hustle, and 2015's Joy.

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:05.780
Lawrence was an undeniable star around the
world by the time she was just 22 years old,

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:10.260
and it's hard not to think that such a speedy
ascent to fame might have been an awful lot

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.180
to handle at such a young age.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:17.310
Beyond her onscreen performances, Lawrence
quickly became one of the most recognizable

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:22.440
figures in Hollywood thanks to her public
persona, which drew a wide variety of reactions

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.930
from the general public as she settled into
stardom.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:30.430
Right off the bat, Lawrence presented herself
as a "cool girl" who would drink to excess,

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.750
make raunchy jokes, and do away with any pretension.

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.470
"And then, I don't know.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.720
Something in me just snapped.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.120
Couldn't have been the alcohol."

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:41.970
For many women, this was a refreshing change
of pace for such a huge celebrity, but as

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:46.220
with all things, the internet backlash followed
swiftly and intensely.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:50.240
Whether Lawrence was putting on an act or
simply being herself, the damage was done,

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:55.390
and the backlash hit hard, with the star being
accused of faking a relatable public persona

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.470
just to score likability points.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:06:01.460
Whether or not her critics had any idea what
they were talking about, that can't have been

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:05.810
an easy thing for Lawrence to endure, and
unfortunately for her, the wave of backlash

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:08.900
preceded some of her least popular film releases.

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:14.930
Flush with industry capital after several
huge early successes, Jennifer Lawrence signed

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:20.530
on to appear in several films that, unfortunately,
didn't bring her much acclaim or success.

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:26.020
She reunited with David O. Russell for the
biopic Joy, which cast Lawrence as the creator

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:27.360
of the Miracle Mop.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.810
Sadly, the movie wasn't received as well as
their previous collaborations.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:37.330
To make matters worse, 2016's X-Men: Apocalypse
also received mediocre reviews, despite a

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:40.440
respectable performance at the box office.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:46.620
Lawrence's final project of 2016, Passengers,
had every ingredient for success on paper,

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:50.730
between its high-concept space setting and
Lawrence's co-star Chris Pratt.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:54.630
Though Pratt and Lawrence both earned praise
for their performances, the film was largely

00:06:54.630 --> 00:07:00.170
disliked, thanks in large part to an unsettling
third act twist, making for a third consecutive

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.040
critical flop for Lawrence.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.001
Following her appearances in several high-profile
critical failures throughout 2016, Lawrence

00:07:08.001 --> 00:07:13.120
returned to her roots in smaller independent
films in 2017.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.790
Unfortunately, this decision didn't quite
pan out either.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:21.870
Lawrence took a huge career leap by taking
on the title role in Darren Aronofsky's mother!,

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:26.090
a disturbing horror film that should have
put her firmly back on the map as an actor

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.310
to watch.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:31.610
When all was said and done, mother! wasn't
the career resurgence Lawrence needed at all,

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:37.080
and as her only film project in 2017, it left
a lasting impression of a career that seemed

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.120
to be on the decline.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:43.790
In the aftermath of mother!'s release, Jennifer
Lawrence returned to big-budget projects,

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.940
which also didn't work out as she likely planned.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:52.420
In 2018, Lawrence headlined the spy drama
Red Sparrow, which cast her as a prima ballerina

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:58.000
who becomes a spy when she's tasked to work
for the original incarnation of the KGB, which

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.570
was known in Russia as the SVR.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:04.360
Despite intense training for the role, Red
Sparrow, which reunited Lawrence with her

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:09.470
Hunger Games director Francis Lawrence — no
relation — performed acceptably at the box

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:12.730
office, but was largely a critical failure.

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:17.030
Lawrence's next project, the X-Men movie Dark
Phoenix, which saw her reprising her role

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:22.450
as the mutant Mystique alongside an ensemble
cast that included Game of Thrones star Sophie

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:25.150
Turner, suffered an even worse fate.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:30.030
Panned by critics and rejected by audiences,
the film became the lowest-grossing entry

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:35.589
in the X-Men franchise, though it was later
unseated by 2020's New Mutants, which was

00:08:35.589 --> 00:08:38.190
released during a global pandemic.

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:42.649
Sadly for Lawrence, her most recent film projects
definitely didn't go as planned, and left

00:08:42.649 --> 00:08:45.029
her with a string of flops in their wake.

00:08:45.029 --> 00:08:46.240
"That just gets me going."

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:50.540
Ultimately, Jennifer Lawrence's break from
public life has more to do with the pandemic

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:52.720
than any major career decisions.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.820
The actress has multiple projects in development,
many of which have been delayed, but will

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:59.329
likely hit our screens in the coming months.

00:08:59.329 --> 00:09:03.870
And any recent career setbacks aside, her
personal life has also taken center stage,

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.670
in good ways as well as bad ones.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:11.720
Lawrence was the subject of a cruel data leak
in 2014, and her friendships with Amy Schumer

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:17.170
and the Kardashian family have been the subject
of tabloid attention, sometimes overshadowing

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:19.740
her impressive artistic accomplishments.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:25.769
In October of 2019, Lawrence wed art gallery
director Cooke Maroney and has been largely

00:09:25.769 --> 00:09:27.310
off the radar since.

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:33.529
However, as E! Online reported in 2018, Lawrence
also just thinks it's healthy to take a break

00:09:33.529 --> 00:09:37.810
from Hollywood once in a while, and she took
a scheduled hiatus that year..

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:43.279
And thanks to this performer's sheer talent,
it's safe to assume she'll return to the big

00:09:43.279 --> 00:09:44.320
screen whenever she wants to.

